// aug22c class A (campaign-minimized): a `let` bound INSIDE a container
// literal that stands as a statement, then a self-connect `x <- x`. The
// interp spins forever (x fires, the RHS reads it, the connect schedules
// the next cycle); the JIT went quiet after the first cycle. The emitter's
// dead-statement elimination scanned for later readers only when the
// statement WAS a `let`, and treated any other statement as unread — the
// literal was eliminated whole, and `x`'s seed (a lifted connect target)
// with it. A statement binds whatever its subtree binds.
{{ b: true, y: let x = true }; x <- x; true}
